WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.910
What drove Sophia Bush and Chad Michael Murray
apart after they fell in love on the set of

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.009
One Tree Hill?

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:11.260
Which classic sitcom star celebrated her on-screen
husband's death with a round of champagne?

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.990
Keep watching, and all will be revealed.

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:18.630
Before he was known as that guy who starred
in all those religious films, Kirk Cameron

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.689
broke big as Mike Seaver on the ABC sitcom
Growing Pains.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:27.609
Alas, when he converted to Christianity near
the end of the show's run, he became a holy

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:28.609
terror.

00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:32.480
There are differing accounts of what exactly
went down between Cameron and his co-star

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.840
Julie McCullough, who played Julie Costello,
but it's clear that neither one liked the

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.300
other very much.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.670
There are two different versions of the story,
though everyone besides Cameron tells the

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:43.929
same one.

00:00:43.929 --> 00:00:49.070
In a 2017 interview with Wingman Magazine,
McCullough claimed that Cameron had her removed

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:54.540
from the show because she'd posed nude in
Playboy, which went against his newfound faith.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.539
He gave her an ultimatum, and that proved
to be the end of her run.

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:02.820
Cameron has never spoken publicly about the
incident, but he was quite controlling on

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.740
the set, which he admitted to in an interview
with CBN.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:10.390
At times, he even forced writers to rewrite
scenes that he deemed immoral.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:15.310
"When you make a decision, like, 'I'm not
comfortable saying that line or doing that

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.040
scene,' well, that meant that 11 writers had
to come up with a new scene."

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.780
Furthermore, he confessed to the Los Angeles
Times in 2000 that he cut off contact with

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.369
his Growing Pains castmates for quite some
time, so it's not too hard to believe that

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:31.060
he used his clout to kick someone off the
show.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.399
As for McCullough, her Twitter feed makes
it quite clear that she's still not a fan

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:37.110
of her former co-star.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:41.170
She called him out in 2017 for his words about
the victims of Hurricane Irma.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:47.020
Ross and Rachel were the couple on Friends
that everyone couldn't stop talking about.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:51.850
But when they were on one of their famous
breaks, Rachel tried to seduce Joshua, played

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.340
by Tate Donovan.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.820
The two eventually had a brief relationship,
but Joshua's arc is mostly remembered for

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.659
the incredibly cringeworthy ways in which
Jennifer Aniston as Rachel tried to seduce

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:03.659
him.

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:07.500
The writing made it uncomfortable, but there
was another factor at play behind the scenes

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.150
that made their relationship even more awkward.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:14.720
Aniston and Donovan had been a couple in real
life, and they'd just broken up when he got

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.330
the call to appear on Friends.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:20.720
He thought this might be a healthy way to
move past the relationship, but he soon discovered

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.690
that the opposite was true.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:27.530
In a 2013 interview with HuffPost Live, he
admitted that filming romantic scenes with

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:30.040
his ex was "horrible," while also noting:

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.750
"I remember just getting back to my dressing
room and just weeping."

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.550
Donovan may have been able to laugh about
it while looking back, but it was clearly

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.884
a bad experience for him at the time.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:45.170
Charlie Sheen isn't exactly known for an even-tempered
demeanor.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:49.870
He was famously fired from Two and a Half
Men in 2011 following a series of bizarre

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.830
comments and behavior, and he quickly made
enemies on his follow-up show as well.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:59.450
FX decided that they could make some money
with a sitcom starring Sheen, so they hired

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.590
him for the aptly-named Anger Management.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:07.760
Working alongside Sheen was Selma Blair, who
played his therapist and part-time lover Kate.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:12.500
Alas, Sheen immediately got up to his old
antics, including showing up late and being

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.340
unprofessional on set.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.060
When Blair brought the issue up, Sheen turned
on her.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.510
As one insider told E!,

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:22.450
"[He] went full throttle into getting her
off the show immediately."

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:27.590
Unsurprisingly for a Charlie Sheen vehicle,
the environment on set was described as "awkward

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.300
and toxic for everyone."

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.420
The real kicker was that Blair reportedly
found out that she was fired via text message.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:39.420
Sometimes, co-stars hit it off right away,
only for their relationship to gradually deteriorate

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.500
over time.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:44.750
But fortunately, Nina Dobrev and Paul Wesley
experienced the complete opposite when they

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.230
starred together on The Vampire Diaries.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:52.620
Dobrev played Elena, who was in a love triangle
with Paul Wesley's Stefan and Ian Somerhalder's

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.620
Damon.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.410
Alas, Dobrev and Wesley clashed immediately.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:04:00.950
They both stayed quiet about it at the time,
but they've talked about it in the years since.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:06.850
During a 2019 appearance on the Directionally
Challenged podcast, for example, Dobrev explained,

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:11.460
"There's a fine line between love and hate,
and we despised each other so much that it

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.960
read as love."

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:17.390
Wesley seconded these thoughts in an interview
with Entertainment Tonight, as he admitted:

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.930
"Creatively, it just wasn't in sync."

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:22.960
Thankfully, this story has a happy ending.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:27.090
The timeline of their reconciliation is a
little wonky, as Dobrev says it only took

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:31.479
a few months, while Wesley claims it took
a few seasons, but regardless, they eventually

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:32.479
became friends.

00:04:32.479 --> 00:04:36.539
They only have praise for each other now,
with both saying that they talk regularly.

00:04:36.539 --> 00:04:38.719
"Now, I just adore her.

00:04:38.719 --> 00:04:39.719
She adores me."

00:04:40.236 --> 00:04:45.380
Pretty much any fan of The X-Files knows that
despite Mulder and Scully's crackling chemistry

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.870
on-screen, the actors who played them didn't
get along off-screen.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:54.110
David Duchovny and Gillian Anderson played
the famous FBI agents on the Fox drama, and

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:58.620
their characters eventually went from professional
partners to romantic pair, to the delight

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.250
of legions of viewers.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:04.699
However, working that closely with one other
person for years can lead to some struggles,

00:05:04.699 --> 00:05:08.280
which Duchovny talked about in a 2008 interview
with Metro.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.840
At that point, he was able to look back fondly
on his time on the show, and he even compared

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.190
Anderson to a sister.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:18.919
However, he also said that "familiarity breeds
contempt," and the two simply got sick of

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:23.110
working together, though he insisted that
it had nothing to do with her specifically.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.460
The intense shooting schedule and serious
subject matter led to petty arguments, and

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:31.520
Duchovny explained that it got to the point
that he and Anderson, quote, "couldn't stand

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:32.909
the sight of each other."

00:05:32.909 --> 00:05:37.220
Thankfully, this is another story with a happy
ending, as the two reunited for an X-Files

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:42.560
reboot in 2016, and they'd clearly gotten
past any animosity, particularly if their

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.610
interview on Jimmy Kimmel Live! from that
year is anything to go by.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.740
"These are people that get along, the two
people that I'm looking at right here."

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.037
"Uh, go on."

00:05:51.573 --> 00:05:56.560
Before there was Ross and Rachel or Mulder
and Scully, TV's ultimate will-they-or-won't-they

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:01.039
couple was Maddie and David on Moonlighting,
who were played by Cybill Shepherd and Bruce

00:06:01.039 --> 00:06:02.699
Willis, respectively.

00:06:02.699 --> 00:06:06.750
Fans tuned in every week to see them solve
cases and flirt with each other.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:11.419
Unfortunately, like so many TV couples with
unresolved romantic tension, things quickly

00:06:11.419 --> 00:06:13.610
went downhill after they resolved it.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:18.210
In 2005, Shepherd told Entertainment Weekly
that Willis was great to work with at first.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.210
As she put it,

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.169
"With Bruce, the temperature in the room went
20 degrees higher.

00:06:22.169 --> 00:06:23.539
For me, anyway."

00:06:23.539 --> 00:06:27.650
However, over time, the two of them simply
began to hate each other.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:32.189
She blamed the mutual dislike on the show's
"volatile" nature, but their co-star Curtis

00:06:32.189 --> 00:06:35.169
Armstrong has claimed that there was more
to the story.

00:06:35.169 --> 00:06:37.550
As he wrote in his book Revenge of the Nerd,

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:42.759
"[Bruce] intimated to me that there had been
one disastrously ill-conceived 'thing' between

00:06:42.759 --> 00:06:45.669
him and Cybill, early on in the show's run.

00:06:45.669 --> 00:06:49.820
While not going into explicit details, he
made it clear that that kind of mistake was

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.960
one I should be sure never to make."

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:57.889
Fortunately, though, Willis and Shepherd eventually
decided that their grudge should die hard

00:06:57.889 --> 00:07:01.849
with a vengeance, and they even reunited at
his Comedy Central Roast in 2018.

00:07:03.509 --> 00:07:07.780
Acting alongside someone you've recently broken
up with is one thing, but acting alongside

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:11.550
your ex-husband who cheated on you is another
entirely.

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:16.849
Alas, that's exactly what Sophia Bush had
to do on the teen drama One Tree Hill.

00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:21.210
She played Brooke Davis, who was in a love
triangle that also involved Chad Michael Murray's

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.210
Lucas Scott.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:27.070
At first, the romantic tension between the
two boiled over happily into real life, as

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:33.289
Bush and Murray quickly got engaged and married,
but it all came crashing down almost immediately.

00:07:33.289 --> 00:07:38.199
The couple said "I do" in April 2005, but
then they split up in September of that same

00:07:38.199 --> 00:07:39.199
year.

00:07:39.199 --> 00:07:44.120
On a 2006 episode of Ryan Seacrest's radio
show, musician Nick Carter alleged that this

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:48.289
was because his ex-girlfriend Paris Hilton
had an affair with Murray.

00:07:48.289 --> 00:07:53.000
Unfortunately for Murray and Bush, they had
to continue working on One Tree Hill together

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.680
until it came to an end in 2012.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:59.939
Bush has since tried to avoid talking about
the incident, but when it did come up during

00:07:59.939 --> 00:08:03.830
a 2021 episode of the Inside of You podcast,
she explained,

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.559
"I'm not going to talk about him.

00:08:05.559 --> 00:08:09.839
I'm not allowed to because I've tried to poke
fun at being a dumb kid and whenever I've

00:08:09.839 --> 00:08:11.729
done that, it gets twisted.

00:08:11.729 --> 00:08:13.020
[...] It's not worth my time.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:14.939
It's not a place where I harbor ill will or
anything."

00:08:16.139 --> 00:08:20.270
Similar to Mulder and Scully, Richard Castle
and Kate Beckett were professional partners

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:23.370
who also had fantastic romantic chemistry.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:28.009
The Castle leads eventually became a couple
and started a family as the seasons went on,

00:08:28.009 --> 00:08:32.780
but the relationship between actors Nathan
Fillion and Stana Katic was apparently not

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.330
quite as rosy.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:38.820
Neither actor has publicly addressed the working
relationship directly, but an insider told

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:43.180
Us Weekly in 2016 that things were indeed
quite difficult on set.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:47.900
Fillion was reportedly so harsh to Katic that
she would cry in her dressing room, and the

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:51.660
two were apparently even forced to attend
counseling sessions together.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:56.540
The show ended in 2016 after eight seasons,
but her departure from it was quite messy.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:09:01.030
First, it was announced that her contract
hadn't been renewed, and then ABC announced

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.230
that the show was ending.

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:07.090
In a 2018 interview with Entertainment Weekly,
Katic addressed her departure by noting,

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:08.790
"It hurt and it was a harsh ending."

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:13.420
However, she did also claim that she was still
overall thankful for the experience.

00:09:14.136 --> 00:09:17.890
Sitcoms wouldn't be what they are today without
I Love Lucy.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:22.320
Lucille Ball was of course the star of the
show, but her co-stars Vivian Vance and William

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:27.070
Frawley, who played Lucy's neighbors Ethel
and Fred Mertz, were also a big part of what

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:28.210
made it so great.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:32.460
The always-bickering couple had fantastic
chemistry, but the fighting didn't end when

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.350
the cameras stopped rolling.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:38.280
Vance was only two years younger than Ball,
but she was playing the wife of a man more

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:40.760
than two decades her senior.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.460
According to the book Meet the Mertzes, Vance
admitted,

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:47.160
"I loathed William Frawley and the feeling
was mutual.

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:50.430
Whenever I received a new script, I raced
through it, praying that there wouldn't be

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.790
a scene where we had to be in bed together."

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:56.310
Frawley in turn didn't have very nice things
to say, as he quipped,

00:09:56.310 --> 00:10:00.450
"She's one of the finest girls to come out
of Kansas, but I often wish she'd go back

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.450
there."

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:05.490
According to an oft-repeated story, which
was recorded in the book The Dead Celebrity

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:10.100
Cookbook, Vance was at a restaurant when she
learned that Frawley had died.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:14.130
Upon hearing the news, she ordered champagne
for everyone.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:19.180
Whether or not this story is true, it accurately
sums up the hostile working relationship between

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.180
the two.

00:10:20.969 --> 00:10:23.680
Martin Lawrence is no stranger to controversy.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:28.320
His infamous Saturday Night Live monologue
in 1994 reportedly got him a lifetime ban

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:29.920
from the show, for example.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:36.070
His sitcom Martin, which ran on Fox from 1992
to 1997, was popular, but also not without

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.070
controversy.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:41.380
A big reason for the show's success was Lawrence's
chemistry with Tisha Campbell, who played

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:42.500
his wife Gina.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:46.370
Alas, things were much rockier when the cameras
weren't rolling.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:50.380
Campbell left the show in the fifth season
and brought legal action against Lawrence

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:57.130
for "repeated and escalating sexual harassment,
sexual battery, verbal abuse and related threats."

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:01.860
The case was ultimately settled out of court,
and Campbell returned for the show's finale.

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:06.221
However, since Lawrence wasn't allowed to
be around her when she shot her scenes, it

00:11:06.221 --> 00:11:07.880
made for an awkward conclusion.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:13.780
In the 2020 interview with GQ, Lawrence claimed
that the sexual harassment, quote, "didn't

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:14.780
happen."

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:18.470
Meanwhile, Campbell revealed on an episode
of The Talk that same year that due to the

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:23.220
settlement agreement, she isn't allowed to
speak about the matter in much detail.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:27.580
If you or anyone you know has been a victim
of sexual assault, help is available.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:33.810
Visit the Rape, Abuse &amp; Incest National Network
website or contact RAINN's National Helpline

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:38.980
at 1-800-656-HOPE (4673).

